## 12. Message to Founder

Hi Yug,

I wanted to give you a Day 4 update on the BoltIQ Strategy Tester
validation.

The main issue today was tester performance. I ran the BoltIQ Gold
Portfolio Engine on XAUUSD M15 for the same approximately 3-month
historical range using 1 Minute OHLC. The test was progressing extremely
slowly --- around 25 minutes for only \~3.6% of the test range, which
projects to roughly 11--12 hours if the speed remains similar.

I investigated the repeated
`MultiScanner: skipped (MaxShortTrades=0, Phase 2 BUY-only mode)`
message in the tester Journal. I traced it to a single `Print()`
statement in the MultiScanner guard. Because this section can be reached
repeatedly from the tick path, I investigated/suppressed the repeated
diagnostic output.

However, after rerunning the same test range, the overall runtime
remained approximately the same.

This suggests that the MultiScanner logging is not the main bottleneck.
Also, because `MaxShortTrades=0`, the actual MultiScanner calculation
branch is skipped, so the BTCUSD/EURUSD/GBPUSD scanner calculations are
not currently the main explanation either.

My current assessment is that the EA is computationally heavy during
historical simulation because of the amount of work connected to the
tick path --- multiple strategies, MTF filters, risk/margin checks,
position/order scans, telemetry, dashboard/export, ONNX-related
processing and other safety gates. I don't want to claim a specific
bottleneck without evidence.

My next step is to trace/profile the main `OnTick()` execution path and
identify which operations are consuming the tester time, while keeping
the production trading and risk logic unchanged.

The key result from today is that we have ruled out the repeated
MultiScanner log as the sole cause and narrowed the problem to the
broader EA/tester workload.

